A||N||4||DJWINNI||IDLE ABOUT 3000-3500 RPM.....||||8||
Z||000000||DJWINNI||12-07-2001||01:07 PM||||Hi! I'm totally lost with my Fiero. My idle problem is still not resolved. In fact, the prob is that my idle is about 3000-3500 RPM, but if I disconnect the plastic hose going from the MAP to the Fuel Pressure Regulation situated underneath th red spider, the idle drops to 1500-2000RPM. All my plastic hoses are good like the EGR tube and the EGR valve is new...Where is the real problem???? Can someone PLEASE help me?<BR>Thanks a lot!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg" TARGET=_blank>pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||PBJ||12-07-2001||07:35 PM||||I would remove the IAC and see if you can move the plunger a wee bit (if not you need a new one).  Have you checked the vacuum with a guage, if not you need to, cause a visual inspection of vacuum lines will likely not reveal a problem.<P>Hope this helps. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-12-2001||12:48 PM||||Try spraying carb cleaner on the vac lines...if the rpm changes....then you have a leak.  Also, check the IAC valve as stated above.<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||12-12-2001||02:38 PM||||Getting any codes?<BR>Service engine light come on at anytime while running?<BR>Throttle position sensor stuck or installed incorrectly? <BR>Throttle return spring missing or broken?<P>Look for the 'out of ordinary' as well.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJWINNI||12-13-2001||08:01 AM||||Thanks a lo for the answers!<BR>I will check all of this this week-end!!<BR>tanksfor your help!!<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg" TARGET=_blank>pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
